1
00:00:00,180 --> 00:00:01,200
Mobility is one of

2
00:00:01,220 --> 00:00:02,320
the strongest predictors

3
00:00:02,340 --> 00:00:03,600
of how well you’ll age.

4
00:00:03,620 --> 00:00:04,640
Starting in our 30s,

5
00:00:04,660 --> 00:00:06,080
we gradually lose muscle mass,

6
00:00:06,100 --> 00:00:07,280
and the loss speeds up

7
00:00:07,300 --> 00:00:08,400
as we get older.

8
00:00:08,420 --> 00:00:09,520
Less muscle mass means

9
00:00:09,540 --> 00:00:10,320
less stability,

10
00:00:10,340 --> 00:00:11,360
slower reactions,

11
00:00:11,380 --> 00:00:13,200
and a higher risk of falls.

12
00:00:13,220 --> 00:00:14,080
The good news is that

13
00:00:14,100 --> 00:00:15,200
it is very trainable

14
00:00:15,220 --> 00:00:16,080
at any age,

15
00:00:16,100 --> 00:00:16,640
but you have to

16
00:00:16,660 --> 00:00:17,840
measure it first.

17
00:00:17,860 --> 00:00:19,120
So when we look at mobility,

18
00:00:19,140 --> 00:00:20,160
we ask three things.

19
00:00:20,180 --> 00:00:22,000
One, can you move with control?

20
00:00:22,020 --> 00:00:23,040
Two, can you maintain

21
00:00:23,060 --> 00:00:24,320
your range of motion?

22
00:00:24,340 --> 00:00:25,680
And three, are you strong enough

23
00:00:25,700 --> 00:00:27,360
for every stage of life?

24
00:00:27,380 --> 00:00:28,640
Mobility isn’t just about

25
00:00:28,660 --> 00:00:29,600
how you move today.

26
00:00:29,620 --> 00:00:30,480
It’s about protecting

27
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:31,600
what you’ll be able to do

28
00:00:31,620 --> 00:00:33,760
10, 20, 30 years from now.

29
00:00:33,780 --> 00:00:34,880
At Vexon Med,

30
00:00:34,900 --> 00:00:35,920
we measure it so we can

31
00:00:35,940 --> 00:00:37,280
build a plan around it.

32
00:00:37,300 --> 00:00:38,480
Click the link in our bio

33
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:39,870
to book your assessment.
